 "narrative": "Estimates are signed to each claimed hypothesis direction, so I judged whether the signed point estimate exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units and whether its uncertainty supports a scientifically meaningful effect. The interaction tests for the large predictors do not support meaningful context modification: H30 SMARCA4-loss interaction by TP53 loss is only -0.070 with interval crossing zero and opposite values; H62 SMARCA4 high-screen-quality interaction is +0.022 in the wrong sign relative to the negative interaction hypothesis; and H63 TP53 high-screen-quality interaction is only +0.027 with interval including zero. These do not support meaningful effect modification beyond threshold, so I reject and close them. This is not proof that no modification exists, but the supplied data do not support it. The PTEN results are mixed. H47 adenocarcinoma PTEN-loss gives a signed +0.227 stronger-dependency contrast, a meaningful point estimate consistent with prior PTEN evidence, though its lower bound falls below the 0.15-unit threshold; I accept it as an active moderate dataset-specific subgroup association pending more mature validation. Other PTEN contexts are less decisive: high screen-quality H65 is +0.192 but lower bound +0.069; high-aneuploidy H66 is +0.271 but lower bound +0.087 and exposed cell is small; TP53-loss H67 is barely above threshold with interval crossing zero; and non-Avana H75 is small-n, below threshold, and wide. Therefore I leave H65/H66/H67 unresolved and deferred, and reject H75. CDKN2A remains borderline at best: high-quality H72 is +0.116, below threshold and not meaningful, so I reject it; Avana H73 is +0.149 and adenocarcinoma H74 is +0.153, both essentially threshold-boundary with intervals not decisively above threshold, so I keep them unresolved and deferred rather than accepting. H78 high-versus-intermediate serum percentage is small and opposite the claimed positive direction, giving no evidence for a meaningful culture-condition association, so I reject and close it. For validation, I request H40 because it is the strongest PTEN evidence: PTEN loss in TP53-wildtype samples has a signed discovery estimate +0.259 with lower bound above threshold. Independent validation of this subgroup claim would clarify whether PTEN loss is a moderately supported dataset-specific association, while overall PTEN remains active but threshold-boundary. No causal or external generalization claim is made.",
 "research_notes": "Current status after new batch: validated/closed large dataset-specific associations remain H3 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency, H13 TP53 loss -> weaker dependency, H38 KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency. Context/interaction tests for the large predictors are closed: H30 no negative SMARCA4-by-TP53 interaction, H62/H63 no screen-quality interactions; H46/H58 earlier interactions already rejected. PTEN remains the key moderate signal but context heterogeneity is evident. Overall H24 is accepted active but lower bound below threshold. TP53-wildtype H40 is the strongest PTEN context with discovery interval entirely above threshold; I requested validation H40. Adenocarcinoma PTEN H47 is accepted active but lower bound below threshold. Other PTEN contexts H65 high-screen-quality, H66 high-aneuploidy, H67 TP53-loss are unresolved/deferred; H75 non-Avana rejected small-n/unsupported; H58 PTEN-by-TP53 interaction rejected. CDKN2A is borderline: overall H4 and TP53-wt H20 unresolved; high-quality H72 rejected; Avana H73 and adenocarcinoma H74 remain unresolved/deferred near threshold. Culture/technical main effects: H78 serum 10 vs 5 rejected/null; H76/H77 method/QC main effects not yet analyzed and remain registered. Next: wait for H40 validation. If H40 validates, PTEN TP53-wt subgroup becomes a validated moderate dataset-specific association and overall PTEN should be reassessed to decide whether to keep it as overall moderate, narrow to TP53-wt, or downgrade. If H40 validation does not clear the threshold independently, PTEN should remain exploratory and H24/H47 may be downgraded. If validation confirms, consider later validation of overall H24 only if the claim set and budget support a broader PTEN claim; otherwise focus final claims on three large validated predictors plus PTEN TP53-wt. All claims remain associations within the supplied dataset, not causal effects or generalizable biological mechanisms.",
